---
description: Security scanning before commits
alwaysApply: true
---

Before running git commit, git push, or creating a PR, call the armis-scanner
MCP tool `scan_diff` with `staged=true`. If HIGH/CRITICAL findings exist,
fix them or ask the user for approval before proceeding.

To suppress a reviewed false positive, add an `armis:ignore` comment on the
finding's line (optionally `armis:ignore cwe:798`) or list it in `.armisignore`
at the repo root. Suppressed CRITICAL still requires approval. See AGENTS.md for
full instructions.
